        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>PIA Technical Standard 100</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = { tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$'], ['\\\\(', '\\\\)']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$'], ['\\\\[', '\\\\]']] } };\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body {\n    margin: 0;\n    min-height: 100%;\n    background: #fff;\n  }\n  body {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    color: #000;\n  }\n  .stage {\n    width: 1650px;\n    height: 2160px;\n    position: relative;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: #fff;\n  }\n  .page {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 200px;\n    top: 122px;\n    width: 1350px;\n    height: 1878px;\n    border: 1.5px solid #111;\n    border-radius: 13px;\n    background: #fff;\n    box-shadow: 18px 16px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.48);\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n  .page-header {\n    height: 332px;\n    padding-top: 163px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .standard {\n    font-size: 37px;\n    line-height: 1.1;\n  }\n  .publication {\n    font-size: 31px;\n    line-height: 1.18;\n    margin-top: 2px;\n  }\n  .date {\n    font-size: 25px;\n    font-weight: 400;\n    line-height: 1.1;\n    margin-top: 2px;\n  }\n  .rule {\n    margin-left: 87px;\n    width: 1223px;\n    border-top: 5px solid #111;\n  }\n  .content {\n    width: 1223px;\n    margin-left: 87px;\n    padding-top: 51px;\n    font-size: 25px;\n    line-height: 1.18;\n  }\n  h1 {\n    font-size: 37px;\n    line-height: 1.13;\n    margin: 0 0 39px 0;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  h2 {\n    font-size: 31px;\n    line-height: 1.12;\n    margin: 0 0 30px 0;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  p {\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n  .intro-text {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n  }\n  .address {\n    margin-bottom: 69px;\n    line-height: 1.21;\n  }\n  .address strong {\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .definitions-title {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n  }\n  .term {\n    margin-bottom: 31px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .term strong {\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .angle {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr;\n    column-gap: 0;\n    margin-bottom: 31px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .angle-label {\n    font-weight: 700;\n    padding-top: 0;\n  }\n  .angle-content {\n    padding-left: 0;\n  }\n  .subterm {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 102px 1fr;\n    margin-bottom: 28px;\n  }\n  .subterm strong {\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .area {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr;\n    margin-top: -2px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n  }\n  .area-label {\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .area-content {\n    padding-left: 0;\n  }\n  .area-content .subterm {\n    grid-template-columns: 204px 1fr;\n    margin-bottom: 27px;\n  }\n  .aspect {\n    margin-top: 30px;\n    line-height: 1.18;\n  }\n  .page-number {\n    position: absolute;\n    bottom: 31px;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 100%;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    font-size: 21px;\n  }\n  .change {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 200px;\n    top: 2030px;\n    font-size: 25px;\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n  .appendix {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 100px;\n    top: 2026px;\n    font-size: 27px;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"stage\">\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <header class=\"page-header\">\n      <div class=\"standard\">PIA Technical Standard 100</div>\n      <div class=\"publication\">Parachute Industry Association Publications</div>\n      <div class=\"date\">March 27, 2015</div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"rule\"></div>\n\n    <section class=\"content\">\n      <h1>Standardized Nomenclature for Ram-Air Parachutes</h1>\n\n      <h2>Introduction</h2>\n\n      <p class=\"intro-text\">\n        This Technical Standard was adopted by the Parachute Industry Association (PIA) on March 27, 2015.<br>\n        Input concerning revisions and additions should be submitted to:\n      </p>\n\n      <div class=\"address\">\n        <strong>Parachute Industry Association, Inc.</strong><br>\n        Attention:&nbsp; Technical Committee Chair<br>\n        3833 West Oakton Street<br>\n        Skokie, IL 60076<br>\n        Telephone: 847-674-9472<br>\n        Fax: 847-674-9743<br>\n        Email:&nbsp; <a href=\"mailto:TechComChair@pia.com\">TechComChair@pia.com</a>\n      </div>\n\n      <h2 class=\"definitions-title\">Definitions</h2>\n\n      <div class=\"term\">\n        <strong>Airlock:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; On a canopy, a valve which permits air flow more easily in one direction, and restricts airflow in<br>\n        the opposite direction.&nbsp;&nbsp; In most case, airlocks are installed in the nose of the canopy to permit air to enter<br>\n        during deployment and flight, and restrict air from flowing out the nose to ensure better pressurization in<br>\n        turbulent air.\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"angle\">\n        <div class=\"angle-label\">Angle of</div>\n        <div class=\"angle-content\">\n          <div class=\"subterm\">\n            <strong>Attack:</strong>\n            <span>The angle formed between the flight path and the chord line.&nbsp; The Greek letter alpha (α)<br>is used to denote the angle of attack.&nbsp; See Figure 3.</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"subterm\">\n            <strong>Trim:</strong>\n            <span>The angle formed between the horizontal reference line and the trim line.&nbsp; The Greek letter<br>theta (θ) is used to denote the angle of trim.&nbsp; Used instead of the somewhat analogous aircraft<br>term “angle of incidence.”&nbsp; See Figure 1b.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"area\">\n        <div class=\"area-label\">Area,</div>\n        <div class=\"area-content\">\n          <div class=\"subterm\">\n            <strong>Airfoil Section:</strong>\n            <span>The finished cross sectional area of a given rib (airfoil) section.&nbsp; When ribs are<br>not identical, the specific rib must be identified. Used for calculations of pack volume and internal<br>volume of canopy.</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"subterm\">\n            <strong>Planform:</strong>\n            <span>The product of the average chord times the average span of the canopy.</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"subterm\">\n            <strong>Projected:</strong>\n            <span>The area of an inflated canopy as viewed from above, perpendicular to the chord line<br>at the centerline of the parachute. Due to canopy curvature and cell inflation bulging the projected<br>area is always smaller than the planform area.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"aspect\">\n        <strong>Aspect Ratio:</strong> Span<sup>2</sup>/Area, which for a rectangular planform reduces to Span/Chord.\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <div class=\"page-number\">Page 1 of 8</div>\n  </main>\n\n  <div class=\"change\">Change 1 (December 2015)</div>\n  <div class=\"appendix\">A-3</div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
